  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Soak the pearl barley in water for 4 hours before cooking. Preheat the oven to 150°C. Heat the olive oil in a wide, shallow pot, add the halved peeled shallots, halved unpeeled garlic heads, quartered kohlrabi and turnip and the celeriac cut into eighths, and roast over medium heat for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally."
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain the barley and place it over the vegetables. Arrange the remaining root vegetables (with their leaves) on top and add the rest of the ingredients. Cover the pot, shake gently to mix and cook over medium heat for about 20 minutes."
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer the covered pot to the oven and bake for 1.5 hours. Check during baking: if the liquid falls below the midpoint of the contents, add a little more."
    }
  ]
